<title>HUNGARY: Hungary three-month bill yield rises to 19.52 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary three-month bill yield rises to 19.52 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of three-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 19.52 percent, up from 19.51 percent at an auction one week ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     16,485.51 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    19.52 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     95.3592 pct</p>
</text>
